    "rational functions"
  ],
  "data": {
    "expression": "(3x^2 + 1)/(2x^2 - x)",
    "var": "x",
    "point": "oo"
  },
  "answer": "3/2",
  "mistakes": [
    {
      "answer": "3",
      "hint": "Divide the numerator and the denominator by x², not just the numerator."
    },
    {
      "answer": "oo",
      "hint": "The numerator and the denominator both grow like x². Compare their leading terms."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Divide every term by the highest power of x in the denominator."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Divide by $x^2$: $\\frac{3 + 1/x^2}{2 - 1/x}$.",
    "As $x \\to \\infty$, $1/x^2 \\to 0$ and $1/x \\to 0$, so the limit is $\\frac{3}{2}$."
  ],
